{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f5bdbc4aecca503f","name":"Vornskr","source":{"id":"source:reference-f5bdbc4aecca503f","title":"Vornskr","revision":22206,"timestamp":"2024-08-31T23:57:15Z","sha256":"c51f736310331428af27a5726247cb98617d724bc76a4f917d2cfee3b71db690","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=22206","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Vornskr&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f5bdbc4aecca503f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Native to the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Myrkr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Myrkr?action=edit&redlink=1"},", the Vornskr is a doglike predator with an innate sensitivity to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," and Force-users. These furred quadrupeds have long legs tipped in sharp claw, powerful jaws filled with deadly fangs and long, whip-like tails tipped with poisonous spines. They are aggressive, fast and incredibly strong for their size. Vornskrs are nocturnal, hunting after dark in packs consisting of between three and five individuals. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One of the Vornskr’s primary prey animals is the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ysalamiri"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ysalamiri","referenceId":"reference:76fbe6787718be60"},", a lizard-like creature that is also native to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Myrkr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Myrkr?action=edit&redlink=1"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ysalamiri"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ysalamiri","referenceId":"reference:76fbe6787718be60"}," project a bubble-shaped field that nullifies the use of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", which makes it difficult for Vornskrs to locate them. Vornskrs sometimes mistake a Force-user for a group of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ysalamiri"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ysalamiri","referenceId":"reference:76fbe6787718be60"},", leading them to attack. The presence of Force-users enrages Vornskrs, a behavior that no amount of training can eliminate.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Vornskr Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Vornskrs are dangerous predators that are widely sought as guard animals. The creatures are incredibly difficult to train and even specimens that are raised in captivity are too wild to be truly domesticated. Vornskrs that have their tails clipped are made somewhat less aggressive by the process but they are also deprived of their paralytic poison as a result of the surgery. Regardless of the method used to domesticate Vornskrs, they will always continue to be agitated by Force-users.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Whether they are encountered in the wild or as part of a security detachment, Vornskrs use their Force abilities to locate and track their prey. They are ferocious animals but nonetheless cunning. They prefer to attack in small groups, using numbers and surprise to knock their opponent off balance before delivering a paralyzing tail lash. Once the foe is immobilized, they move in for the kill as a group. When facing multiple adversaries, a pack of Vornskrs pair off and attempt to disable those individuals that seem most threatening. If the tide turns against them, they retreat and regroup, returning only if they are trained to do so.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["On their home planet of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Myrkr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Myrkr?action=edit&redlink=1"},", Vornskr are most often encountered after dark when they are hunting for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ysalamiri"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ysalamiri","referenceId":"reference:76fbe6787718be60"},". They spend the daylight hours asleep, with a single member of the pack left awake to keep watch.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Vornskr Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 7\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +6; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," +8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 18 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 13, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 52, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 13\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 8 Squares\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]}," Bite +8 (1d6+6)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]}," Bite +6 (2d6+6) with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Strike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki